      "text": [
        " \"صَاحِبُ اَلْبُخْتِيِّ ضَامِنٌ لِلدِّيَةِ وَ يَقْبِضُ ثَمَنَ بُخْتِيِّهِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5369 - Hammad narrated from Al-Halabi, who narrated from Abu Abdullah (as), that he was asked about a male camel (bukhti) that became enraged, left the house, and killed a man. Then the brother of the man came and struck the camel with a sword, injuring it.\nImam (as) said: \"The owner of the camel is liable for the blood money, and he is entitled to receive the price of his camel.\""
        ]
      }
